ate/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-ih_qxv51/retort-41b9cc4b5914/src/normalizer.ts\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-ih_qxv51/retort-41b9cc4b5914/src/normalizer.ts\n@@ -97,8 +97,10 @@\n 'AMÉRICA MINEIRO': 'America Mineiro',\n 'AMÉRICA MG': 'America Mineiro',\n 'AMERICA MG': 'America Mineiro',\n 'AMÉRICA-RN': 'America RN',\n+'ATLÉTICO': 'Atletico Mineiro',\n+'ATLETICO': 'Atletico Mineiro',\n 'PONTE PRETA': 'Ponte Preta',\n 'ASSOCIAÇÃO ATLÉTICA PONTE PRETA': 'Ponte Preta',\n 'FLAMENGO RJ': 'Flamengo',\n 'BOTAFOGO RJ': 'Botafogo',\n","additions":2,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"src/normalizer.ts","time":{"start":1782353434039,"end":1782353434042}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The Brasileirao_Matches.csv uses \"Atletico\" for some matches and \"Atletico Mineiro\" for others, even in the same season! That's inconsistent within the same source. So I need to map \"Atletico\" to \"Atletico Mineiro\" to consolidate them. But that would also affect \"Atlético Paranaense\" if it appears as \"Atletico\". However, \"Athletico Paranaense\" is the modern name and usually distinct. In older data, \"Atlético Paranaense\" might appear with \"-PR\". I think it's safe to map plain \"Atletico\" (without state suffix) to \"Atletico Mineiro\" because in the Brasileirão dataset, the matches are clearly Atlético Mineiro (they play in Belo Horizonte, and we can see \"Atletico Mineiro\" vs \"Atletico\" in same season, which is a self-match indicator of inconsistency).\n\nBut wait, the sample shows a match: homeTeam \"Atletico Mineiro\" vs awayTeam \"Atletico\" in 2019. That's clearly the same team. So yes, map plain \"Atletico\" to \"Atletico Mineiro\".\n\nAlso \"Csa\" should map to \"CSA\". Let me add overrides.\n\nAlso, I notice \"America MG\" vs \"America Mineiro\" etc. I already have overrides. Good.\n\nLet me add 'ATLETICO': 'Atletico Mineiro' and 'CSA': 'CSA' overrides. Actually 'Csa' -> 'CSA' via override.\n\nAlso need to handle case where state suffix removal produces 'Atletico' from 'Atletico-MG' but that's already handled by raw override for 'ATLETICO-MG'. But 'Atletico' alone appears in source as raw, so raw override will catch it.\n\nWait, but what if a team is literally called \"Atlético Paranaense\" and appears as \"Atlético\"? That would be wrong. But given the data, it seems \"Atletico\" is only Atlético Mineiro. I'll add it.\n\nAlso \"Csa\" -> \"CSA\".\n\nLet me update normalizer and rebuild/test.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efc8b0777001lQTtiVpT136XIm","sessionID":"ses_1038a1a43ffeeWzYwhyWkjkoD2","messageID":"msg_efc8ad22b001pd02AHPrDXXsA1"}}
