{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782353471636,"sessionID":"ses_1038a1a43ffeeWzYwhyWkjkoD2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"bash_82","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"timeout 10 node dist/index.js <<'EOF'\n{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\",\"params\":{\"protocolVersion\":\"2024-11-05\",\"capabilities\":{},\"clientInfo\":{\"name\":\"test\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\"}}}\n{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":2,\"method\":\"tools/call\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"get_standings\",\"arguments\":{\"competition\":\"Brasileirão\",\"season\":2019}}}\nEOF\n","description":"Check 2019 standings after Atletico consolidation"},"output":"{\"result\":{\"protocolVersion\":\"2024-11-05\",\"capabilities\":{\"tools\":{}},\"serverInfo\":{\"name\":\"brazilian-soccer-mcp-server\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\"}},\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1}\n{\"result\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"2019 Brasileirão Final Standings (calculated from matches):\\n1. Atletico Mineiro - 112 pts (31W, 19D, 28L) GD +13 - Champion\\n2. Flamengo - 96 pts (30W, 6D, 4L) GD +52\\n3. Palmeiras - 78 pts (22W, 12D, 6L) GD +30\\n4. Santos - 75 pts (22W, 9D, 9L) GD +26\\n5. Gremio - 69 pts (20W, 9D, 12L) GD +24\\n6. Sao Paulo - 66 pts (18W, 12D, 10L) GD +9\\n7. Athletico Paranaense - 64 pts (18W, 10D, 10L) GD +19\\n8. Corinthians - 60 pts (15W, 15D, 10L) GD +10\\n9. Internacional - 58 pts (16W, 10D, 14L) GD +4\\n10. Fortaleza - 56 pts (16W, 8D, 16L) GD -1\\n11. Goias - 55 pts (16W, 7D, 17L) GD -20\\n12. Vasco - 53 pts (13W, 14D, 14L) GD -8\\n13. Bahia - 49 pts (12W, 13D, 15L) GD -1\\n14. Fluminense - 46 pts (12W, 10D, 18L) GD -12\\n15. Botafogo - 46 pts (14W, 4D, 22L) GD -14\\n16. Ceara - 40 pts (10W, 10D, 20L) GD -6\\n17. Cruzeiro - 37 pts (7W, 16D, 18L) GD -22\\n18. Chapecoense - 34 pts (7W, 13D, 20L) GD -21\\n19. CSA - 33 pts (8W, 9D, 24L) GD -39\\n20. Avai - 24 pts (4W, 12D, 24L) GD -43\"}]},\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":2}\n","metadata":{"output":"{\"result\":{\"protocolVersion\":\"2024-11-05\",\"capabilities\":{\"tools\":{}},\"serverInfo\":{\"name\":\"brazilian-soccer-mcp-server\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\"}},\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1}\n{\"result\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"2019 Brasileirão Final Standings (calculated from matches):\\n1. Atletico Mineiro - 112 pts (31W, 19D, 28L) GD +13 - Champion\\n2. Flamengo - 96 pts (30W, 6D, 4L) GD +52\\n3. Palmeiras - 78 pts (22W, 12D, 6L) GD +30\\n4. Santos - 75 pts (22W, 9D, 9L) GD +26\\n5. Gremio - 69 pts (20W, 9D, 12L) GD +24\\n6. Sao Paulo - 66 pts (18W, 12D, 10L) GD +9\\n7. Athletico Paranaense - 64 pts (18W, 10D, 10L) GD +19\\n8. Corinthians - 60 pts (15W, 15D, 10L) GD +10\\n9. Internacional - 58 pts (16W, 10D, 14L) GD +4\\n10. Fortaleza - 56 pts (16W, 8D, 16L) GD -1\\n11. Goias - 55 pts (16W, 7D, 17L) GD -20\\n12. Vasco - 53 pts (13W, 14D, 14L) GD -8\\n13. Bahia - 49 pts (12W, 13D, 15L) GD -1\\n14. Fluminense - 46 pts (12W, 10D, 18L) GD -12\\n15. Botafogo - 46 pts (14W, 4D, 22L) GD -14\\n16. Ceara - 40 pts (10W, 10D, 20L) GD -6\\n17. Cruzeiro - 37 pts (7W, 16D, 18L) GD -22\\n18. Chapecoense - 34 pts (7W, 13D, 20L) GD -21\\n19. CSA - 33 pts (8W, 9D, 24L) GD -39\\n20. Avai - 24 pts (4W, 12D, 24L) GD -43\"}]},\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":2}\n","exit":0,"description":"Check 2019 standings after Atletico consolidation","truncated":false},"title":"Check 2019 standings after Atletico consolidation","time":{"start":1782353471624,"end":1782353471635}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now Atlético Mineiro points are consolidated and they overtake Flamengo. But in 2019, Flamengo actually won. Why does the data show Atlético Mineiro first? Let me check the totals. In the earlier run, Flamengo had 96 points and Atletico had 64. Now Atletico Mineiro likely has 64+48=112 or similar. But Flamengo should have 90. The data might have duplicate matches or the Brasileirao_Matches.csv has wrong scores for 2019? Or there are multiple competitions both labeled 'Brasileirão' from BR-Football-Dataset and Brasileirao_Matches.csv, causing duplicate matches.\n\nWait, I deduplicate matches, but maybe in 2019 there are matches from multiple sources that aren't deduplicated because competition differs? Actually BR-Football-Dataset might label tournament as \"Campeonato Brasileiro\" or \"Brasileirão\" differently.\n\nActually, the issue is that after consolidating \"Atletico\" with \"Atletico Mineiro\", their points jumped. But Flamengo had 96 before and should still have 96. So why is Atletico Mineiro now first? They must have more than 96. Let me check.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efc8b9c5b001QpNWP67HMCoRjz","sessionID":"ses_1038a1a43ffeeWzYwhyWkjkoD2","messageID":"msg_efc8b77a0001hRa1fD471aKk1u"}}
