{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782353645600,"sessionID":"ses_1038a1a43ffeeWzYwhyWkjkoD2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"bash_97","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"node -e \"\nimport { normalizeTeamName } from './dist/normalizer.js';\nconsole.log(normalizeTeamName('Atletico-MG'));\nconsole.log(normalizeTeamName('Atletico-PR'));\nconsole.log(normalizeTeamName('Athletico-PR'));\n\"","description":"Check Atletico suffix normalization"},"output":"Atletico Mineiro\nAtletico Mineiro\nAthletico Paranaense\n","metadata":{"output":"Atletico Mineiro\nAtletico Mineiro\nAthletico Paranaense\n","exit":0,"description":"Check Atletico suffix normalization","truncated":false},"title":"Check Atletico suffix normalization","time":{"start":1782353645597,"end":1782353645599}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Ah! The raw data has both \"Atletico-MG\" (Atlético Mineiro) and \"Atletico-PR\" (Athletico Paranaense). My suffix stripping removed \"-MG\" and \"-PR\", then the override for \"Atletico\" maps to \"Atletico Mineiro\". So Athletico Paranaense matches are incorrectly mapped to Atlético Mineiro! That's why Atletico Mineiro has 74 matches.\n\nThis is a problem. I should NOT map plain \"Atletico\" to \"Atletico Mineiro\" because \"Atletico-PR\" becomes \"Atletico\" after suffix stripping. I need to handle this differently.\n\nBetter approach: When stripping suffixes, if the suffix is -MG, -PR, -GO, etc., we should map based on the suffix. Or, the override for \"Atletico-MG\" and \"Atletico-PR\" should be applied BEFORE suffix stripping. I already try raw override first, but \"Atletico-PR\" raw override key is \"ATLETICO-PR\" which maps to \"Athletico Paranaense\". Wait, that should work! Why did it become \"Atletico\"?\n\nLet me check normalizeTeamName('Atletico-PR').","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efc8e4b65001bu0UBz4sxD26GI","sessionID":"ses_1038a1a43ffeeWzYwhyWkjkoD2","messageID":"msg_efc8e26e1