ÉTICO PR': 'Athletico Paranaense',\n- 'ATHLÉTICO-PR': 'Athletico Paranaense',\n- 'ATHLETICO-PR': 'Athletico Paranaense'\n\nBut no 'ATLETICO-PR' (with hyphen, no 'H'). So when I stripped diacritics from 'ATLÉTICO-PR', it becomes 'ATLETICO-PR', which is not in the map. Then suffix stripping removes '-PR', leaving 'Atletico', which maps to 'Atletico Mineiro'.\n\nI need to add 'ATLÉTICO-PR' -> 'Athletico Paranaense' and also 'ATLETICO-PR' raw key. Since the map is pre-diarcitic-removed, I should add 'Atlético-PR'.\n\nBut more importantly, I should remove the plain 'Atletico' -> 'Atletico Mineiro' mapping because it causes false positives after suffix stripping.\n\nAlternatively, I can keep 'Atletico' mapping only when no suffix was stripped. But my current logic tries raw override first, then suffix stripping, then stripped override. So if raw 'Atletico-PR' maps correctly, it won't reach 'Atletico' override. The problem is just that 'Atletico-PR' wasn't in overrides.\n\nSo fix: add 'Atlético-PR' to overrides and remove plain 'Atletico' -> 'Atletico Mineiro' (or keep it with caution). Actually I need plain 'Atletico' mapping because Brasileirao_Matches.csv uses plain \"Atletico\" for Atlético Mineiro. But after suffix stripping, 'Atletico-PR' would become 'Atletico' and incorrectly map. However, if raw 'Atletico-PR' maps correctly, it won't reach stripped. So I can keep plain 'Atletico' mapping.\n\nLet me add 'Atlético-PR' override. Also maybe 'Atletico-PR' (without diacritic) but the raw value is diacritic-stripped anyway. Since I pre-process keys with removeDiacritics, adding 'Atlético-PR' covers both.\n\nAlso for 'Atletico-GO' -> 'Atletico Goianiense'. I have 'Atlético Clube Goianiense' and 'Atlético Goianiense' but not 'Atlético-GO'. Add it.\n\nAlso 'América-MG' etc. I have 'América MG' and 'America MG' but not 'América-MG'. Add.\n\nLet me update overrides.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efc8e891f001HTh7wIVaWsnwG6","sessionID":"ses_1038a1a43ffeeWzYwhyWkj