{"type":"text","timestamp":1782353920990,"sessionID":"ses_1038a1a43ffeeWzYwhyWkjkoD2","part":{"id":"prt_efc926e87001ZjgVAw96aL7c6R","messageID":"msg_efc924f71001DW7VuXJ2oC8Ago","sessionID":"ses_1038a1a43ffeeWzYwhyWkjkoD2","type":"text","text":"Implemented the Brazilian Soccer MCP Server in TypeScript. Here's what was built:\n\n**Project structure**\n- `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `jest.config.cjs`, `.gitignore`\n- `src/` modules: `types.ts`, `normalizer.ts`, `loader.ts`, `engine.ts`, `formatter.ts`, `server.ts`, `index.ts`\n- Comprehensive test suite: `*.test.ts` files covering normalizer, loader, engine, formatter, server, and sample questions\n- Updated `README.md`\n\n**Capabilities**\n- Loads all 6 CSV datasets from `data/kaggle/`\n- Normalizes team names, dates, and competitions across sources\n- Exposes 8 MCP tools:\n  - `search_matches`\n  - `get_team_record`\n  - `get_head_to_head`\n  - `search_players`\n  - `get_standings`\n  - `get_statistics`\n  - `list_metadata`\n  - `player_clubs_summary`\n\n**Verification**\n- `npm run build` ✅\n- `npm run lint` ✅\n- `npm test` ✅ — 67 tests passing across 6 suites\n- Smoke-tested the built stdio server with initialize and tool calls\n\nThe server is ready to run via `npm start`.","time":{"start":1782353915527,"end":1782353920983}}}
